<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  camt.053.001.08 (ISO 20022 version 2019). Same element names as the .04
  above, different namespace — this file exists to prove the parser reads both
  without a flag, which is the whole point of matching on local names.

  It also carries the awkward shapes, deliberately:
    Ntry 1  batch booking (Sammelbuchung): two TxDtls under one entry, both
            repeating the entry's AcctSvcrRef — they must not collapse into one
    Ntry 2  PDNG, announced but not booked — skipped by default
    Ntry 3  debit with a SCOR reference
    Ntry 4  reversal of a credit: the money moves the other way
    Ntry 5  no TxDtls at all — some banks put everything on the entry
  Sts and BookgDt use the 2019 shapes (<Sts><Cd>, <DtTm>).

  All names, IBANs and references are PLACEHOLDERS; IID 99999 is not issued.
-->
